<title>UK: Britain's OFT weighs study into dockyard merger.</title>
<headline>Britain's OFT weighs study into dockyard merger.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Office of Fair Trading said on Wednesday it was considering a possible investigation under the country's merger regulations into the proposed aquisition by an Anglo-U.S. consortium of Devonport Royal Dockyards Plc.</p>
<p>The consortium comprises engineering firms BICC Plc and Weir Group Plc, and U.S. energy sevices supplier Halliburton Holdings.</p>
<p>The OFT said in a statement it was inviting representations about the implications for competition and other aspects of the public interest to see if further investigation is warranted.</p>
</text>
